{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require processed meat products to have a carcinogenic warning label",
        "additional_details": "The WHO\u2019s IARC classifies processed meat as a Group 1 carcinogen (like tobacco) and confirms it causes bowel cancer. According to the WHO, eating 50g daily increases bowel cancer risk by 18%, and Cancer Research UK estimates 13% of UK bowel cancers are caused by processed meat. Bowel cancer is the UK\u2019s 4th most common cancer, with 48,200 cases yearly. Cases among 25\u201349-year-olds have risen around 22% since the early 1990s. We believe consumers have a right to know the health risks of processed meat.",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to introduce mandatory, front-of-pack cancer warning labels on processed meat products sold to inform consumers that regular consumption can increase the risk of bowel cancer.",
        "closed_at": null,
